  "plan": {
    "goal": "Design an alveolar-capillary barrier chip under the very low physiological shear of the lung alveolus (~0.03 Pa), using A549 alveolar epithelium.",
    "rationale": "Target the alveolar-capillary shear of ~0.03 Pa (mid-range of the A549 physiological shear window 0.02-0.05 Pa from the physiology registry). A 400 µm wide x 100 µm high x 20 mm long PDMS channel at 1.2 µL/min delivers 0.03 Pa wall shear (verified via flow_rate_for_shear_stress and wall_shear_stress), Re = 0.08 (deeply laminar), pressure drop = 12 Pa (trivial for a syringe pump), residence time = 40 s. A549 seeded at 10,000 cells/cm² on the 0.08 cm² channel floor = 800 cells/channel. O2 supply at 1.2 µL/min is ~250x the epithelial demand (no hypoxia). 16 biological replicates per group for a 1:1 effect:SD comparison at 80% power. A549 is a modest-barrier alveolar line (no model TEER in registry); for a true alveolar-capillary barrier a co-culture with endothelium or a primary alveolar line should be considered.",
