    "caveats": [
      "A549 is a modest-barrier alveolar line with no model TEER in the registry; verify barrier integrity empirically (e.g. FITC-dextran flux) before interpreting transport data.",
      "For a true alveolar-capillary barrier, consider co-culturing A549 with an endothelial line (e.g. HUVEC) on the opposite membrane; this design models the alveolar epithelium alone.",
      "Confirm the syringe pump delivers 1.2 µL/min accurately at this low flow; use a low-dead-volume line and prime to avoid pulsation.",
      "Verify medium viscosity ~1e-3 Pa·s at 37 °C; serum-containing medium may be slightly higher.",
      "A549 doubling 20-26 h; over 72 h the monolayer may over-confluence — monitor and consider shorter culture or lower seeding.",
      "O2 supply is ~250x demand at this flow, so no hypoxia; but confirm the chip material (PDMS) does not deplete O2 or bind the test compound."
